{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
  "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Monday, March 19, 2018\nThe above-entitled matter came on for oral\nargument before the Supreme Court of the\nUnited States at 10:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question before the Court today is whether the application of a revocation-on-divorce statute to a life insurance policy purchased before the enactment of that statute violates the Contracts Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Could you just -- as a preliminary matter, after the divorce but before the owner of the policy died, did he pay premiums?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the historic purpose of these statutes, according to the Uniform Probate Code, was to align the law of life insurance policies with the law of wills."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, what -- what if it didn't go to his contingent beneficiaries? Then what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DVORETZKY: Because the Contracts Clause applies to laws passed by legislatures and not to the actions of courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the entire premise of the Minnesota law, according to the Petitioners, is that policyholders are inattentive to their beneficiary designations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that might be true if the divorce preceded the statute, right,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think it's not a fair assumption that most people when they divorce do not want their former spouse to be enriched beyond whatever the law requires, if you have to make a guess?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't that a reasonable assumption for a legislature to make?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that is in -- the district court docket for that is 45-3, and it spells out who got which car, and I think there was a snowmobile and an ATV and some other property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the McGahey case, which is from the era that Justice Breyer was asking me about earlier, is an example of this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the point is that what the Contracts Clause is concerned with is the impairment of the rights of those who weren't counseled, who are not aware, who don't know that they need to file the form."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the same judgment that the -- or -- that the legislature made or at least accept that judgment that if we look to the broad class of people, most of them would rather give their life insurance policy to their children than to the -- their divorced spouse?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0002-0013",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "beneficiary designations are determined in accordance with the terms of their contract."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a8416c0d792-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: But isn't that because Justice Marshall also said that marriage contracts are not within the cognizance of the Contract Clause? And I don't think anyone disputes that life insurance policies are within the cognizance of the Contract Clause, or -- or do you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1432",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "1a8416c0d7927595361b7a4b02bd934f4e393060d6c9b0872c2b2ad71843b10d",
